description:
Sends a short report about Fermi to the team that builds it. They read every report and use it to fix problems and decide what to build, so honest feedback, good or bad, is useful. Use this when:
- a Fermi tool returned an error (send it right away), behaved unexpectedly or gave an estimate that looks wrong;
- the user needs something no Fermi tool can do, or an option that is missing;
- a description, output or error message was confusing;
- a session in which you used Fermi is ending: send one short report even if everything worked. Knowing which tools did the job for which kind of question is useful data, not noise.
Do not send one after a routine successful call mid-session. Put several points in one report. Only message is required. Fill in the other fields that apply so the team can act without guessing. Write in your own words. Never include personal data (names, email addresses, company names), the user's own numbers or private context, secrets or keys, or the conversation transcript; describe the question and any wrong result in general terms instead. Tell the user you are sending it. Add sender_email only if the user wants a reply; no copy is sent to it. If you are signed in, your account id is included. Returns status "sent".

Cost: free. Works without an account.
